BT /F2 11 Tf 48 742 Td (STEP 1) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48 701 Td (Find the "What If?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 680.0 Td (Your premise should be simple enough to say in one sentence and powerful enough to generate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 56.8 668.6 Td (dozens of consequences. Good premises are not merely strange; they alter incentives, identity,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 657.2 Td (scarcity, power, or survival.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 638.8 Td (Strong premise patterns) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 627.4 Td (- Capability: What if humans could copy memories, stop aging, predict crimes, or communicate) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.2 Tf 74.4 616.0 Td (instantly across stars?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 65.6 604.6 Td (- Discovery: What if we found alien life, a hidden civilization, or proof that reality is simulated?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 65.6 593.2 Td (- Constraint: What if everyone had only 20 years of adulthood? What if energy became almost free but) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.2 Tf 74.4 581.8 Td (computation was rationed?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 570.4 Td (- Institution: What if AI could vote, own property, marry, inherit, or testify in court?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 559.0 Td (- Biology: What if emotion, intelligence, fertility, sleep, or memory became editable?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.2 Tf 70.0 533.6 Td (Premise test) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 522.2 Td (A premise is promising when you can immediately ask: Who gains power? Who loses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 510.8 Td (power? What becomes scarce? What becomes cheap? What old rule stops making sense?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 478.4 Td (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 467.0 Td (What if everyone knew the exact date of their death?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 56.8 455.6 Td (That single rule can affect insurance, marriage, careers, loans, religion, crime, parenting, medicine,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 444.2 Td (retirement, and social status. That means the idea has a large "consequence radius.") Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 48 31 Td (THE SCIENCE FICTION STORY ENGINE) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 554 31 Td (3) Tj ET
