BT /F2 16 Tf 48 701 Td (Know the Question Beneath the Plot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 56.8 680.0 Td (The best science fiction often ends with the audience debating the premise rather than merely) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 56.8 668.6 Td (remembering the action. Decide which human question your fictional system makes impossible to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 657.2 Td (avoid.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 638.8 Td (- What makes a person a person?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 627.4 Td (- Does a perfect copy have the same moral value as the original?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 616.0 Td (- How much freedom should people trade for safety?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 604.6 Td (- Does immortality increase the value of life or destroy it?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 593.2 Td (- If suffering can be removed, should all suffering be removed?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 581.8 Td (- Who deserves power over technology that affects everyone?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 570.4 Td (- If prediction becomes nearly perfect, does responsibility still make sense?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 65.6 559.0 Td (- Can love survive perfect knowledge of another person?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.2 Tf 70.0 533.6 Td (Do not preach the answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 522.2 Td (A strong story usually makes both sides of its central dilemma intelligent. If one side is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 510.8 Td (obviously stupid or evil, the philosophical question collapses into a lecture.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 478.4 Td (A useful final check) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 56.8 467.0 Td (Ask: After finishing my story, what ordinary part of today's world might the reader see differently? If) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 455.6 Td (your future changes how the reader sees the present, the science fiction is doing more than) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 444.2 Td (entertaining.) Tj ET
