BT /F2 11 Tf 48 742 Td (WORKSHEET) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48 701 Td (One-Page Science Fiction Story Engine) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 680.0 Td (Fill this out before writing chapters. Short, sharp answers are better than paragraphs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 661.6 Td (1. WHAT IF?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 650.2 Td (One sentence describing the change to reality.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 624.8 Td (2. THE RULE NOBODY CAN BREAK) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 613.4 Td (The most important limitation, cost, or boundary.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 588.0 Td (3. WHO GAINS / WHO LOSES?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 576.6 Td (Name the groups whose incentives change.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 551.2 Td (4. UNEXPECTED CONSEQUENCE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 539.8 Td (Something most people would not predict at first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 514.4 Td (5. MAIN CHARACTER) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 503.0 Td (Who is positioned at the worst possible intersection of this system?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 477.6 Td (6. WHAT THEY WANT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 466.2 Td (Keep it human and emotionally simple.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 440.8 Td (7. WHAT STOPS THEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 429.4 Td (Make the speculative premise itself part of the obstacle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 404.0 Td (8. WORST THING THAT CAN HAPPEN) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 392.6 Td (What would destroy what they care about most?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 367.2 Td (9. FINAL IMPOSSIBLE CHOICE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 355.8 Td (Two meaningful values; no clean option.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 330.4 Td (10. THE QUESTION LEFT BEHIND) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 56.8 319.0 Td (The idea readers should still be arguing about tomorrow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 48 31 Td (THE SCIENCE FICTION STORY ENGINE) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 554 31 Td (9) Tj ET
