BT /F2 16 Tf 48 701 Td (The "Is This Ready to Write?" Test) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48 680 Td (I can explain the premise in one sentence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 652.0 Td (The speculative element has clear limits and costs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 633.6 Td (I have followed at least three second-order consequences.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 615.2 Td (The world changes incentives, not just scenery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 596.8 Td (My protagonist wants something understandable even without the science fiction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 578.4 Td (The premise makes that desire harder to achieve.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 560.0 Td (The antagonist or opposing force has a rational point of view.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.2 Tf 96.4 541.6 Td (Escalation removes easy solutions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 523.2 Td (The climax requires a meaningful sacrifice or value judgment.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 504.8 Td (The ending shows consequences rather than simply stopping after the action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 486.4 Td (The story leaves a question worth discussing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 96.4 468.0 Td (Removing the science-fiction premise would substantially destroy the story.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.2 Tf 70.0 442.6 Td (The simplest version of the entire manual) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 431.2 Td (Invent one change. Give it rules. Follow the consequences. Find the person it hurts most.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 419.8 Td (Give that person something precious to lose. Escalate until every easy answer disappears.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 70.0 408.4 Td (End with a choice that reveals what the story is really about.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 48 31 Td (THE SCIENCE FICTION STORY ENGINE) Tj ET
